{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries","id":626091,"title":"Are Strix the hypothetical \"splat sponsor\" from Imperial Mysteries?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-13T18:10:31-07:00","id":626091,"title":"Are Strix the hypothetical \"splat sponsor\" from Imperial Mysteries?","content":"...or connected to them? As the B&amp;S references grow, has there been any indication this is the case? Have there been any clarifications of their identity beyond what was present in 1.0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 08-13-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:12:17-07:00","id":626113,"title":"","content":"I never read Imperial Mysteries. What's a splat sponsor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:17:01-07:00","id":626116,"title":"","content":"I don't think they are, they seem like vampires of another sort. They may be related to it.<br /> <br /> @Charlaquin Luna is to the Uratha, the Principle is to Prometheans, sort of a representative in the higher realms used to explain why archmages can't just, 'No more vampires.'<br /> <br /> As for who it might be, the clan books suggest at a great many dark and powerful progenitors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:18:38-07:00","id":626117,"title":"","content":"Whatever fundamental cosmic Archmage-plus level intelligence wants there to be vampires in the first place- their progenitor(s) or creators. The Supernal equivalent of the actual entity Caine.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd. Dammit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:30:45-07:00","id":626125,"title":"","content":"I would argue the strix seem too capricious and venal to be the force preventing the Imperial Archmasters from lifting the Curse from the history of man, but they may be akin in nature. The deep things encountered by the Brothers Worm, the cave-dwelling thing glimpsed by Frances Black, the Mother of Monsters: the history of the Kindred is rife with rumors of distant connections to something hungry dwelling within a deep darkness, perhaps of the sort that potent strix learn to descend into.<br /> <br /> If there is any specific thing in the books likely to be a player in the Imperial Game, I would say it's that outer darkness. Not any one thing out of it, though perhaps some tales of great things like the Mother of Monsters might reflect encounters with the darkness collectively, conflated into a single being. But there is some darkness eating at the world, and the consequences of its presence are what prevent archmages from expelling its influence.<br /> <br /> You might call that the Curse.<br /> <br /> You might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:41:21-07:00","id":626133,"title":"","content":"Not an official term (obviously I hope), but a &quot;splat sponsor&quot; is something that keeps Archmasters from messing with other templates, Luna for Werewolves perhaps, God Machine, Death Gods, etc.*<br /> <br /> Nothing says there is just one sponsor, so whatever first sent the Strix out from wherever they came from could fit the bill. Some unknown thing that lives in the Strix realm that is unable to leave could fit the bill too. Whatever sponsors vampires doesn't seem interested in directly dealing with vampires on a large scale.<br /> <br /> *as stated by others","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T01:39:37-07:00","id":626431,"title":"","content":"There hasn't been an answer, and there probably isn't going to be one. It's a question that only makes sense in terms of Awakening cosmology, and the lines generally ignore each others cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T02:31:53-07:00","id":626443,"title":"","content":"I have to agree, the strix might very well be related to the sponsors who stop archmasters from turning all vampires into lawnchairs, but the strix themselves have neither the temperament or the power to be the sponsor themselves. <br /> <br /> Might be a planet eating ArchStrix somewhere in the lower depths.....<br /> <br /> Of course other options could be God, the God-Machine, the Serpent from the garden of eden, the greco-roman gods, the blood gods, the Dark Mother, Satan, various other deities, Fear, the Crone, and that's just off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T02:42:36-07:00","id":626446,"title":"","content":"Whatever it is, it's content to just let vampires do their thing without interference.<br /> <br /> Maybe they haven't actually got one, but for some reason everyone just sort of assumes they do, and doesn't want to risk pissing it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T03:22:00-07:00","id":626470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries#post626091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or connected to them? As the B&amp;S references grow, has there been any indication this is the case? Have there been any clarifications of their identity beyond what was present in 1.0?</div> </div> </div> </div> While I won't say that they're unconnected, I certainly wouldn't put the strix as the equivalent of Luna and the Firstborn in this case. Thematically, vampire sponsors would be Dracula, Longinus/God*, the Crone*, Belial, and any other major other covenant founders. <br /> <br /> Origin stories of vampires (most notably, Lilith and Ishtar, Durga) involve the strix at a few points, so we could classify these gods as matrons of the vampire race as well. <br /> <br /> <br /> * Could be interesting to have God be the God-Machine and Theban run off Infrastructure (need sacrifices to produce essence to make things happen!) and the Crone could be the same Dark Mother from Beast the Primordial. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T03:44:17-07:00","id":626475,"title":"","content":"Given Mage's platonic cosmology, Vampires wouldn't <i>need</i> a sponsor per se. The Supernal is an expanded world of forms, or ideas at their purest, most perfect form. Vampires could be perceived as a corruption of the idea of Humanity. Vampires could be the hubris of the Exarchs' actions (provided they have indeed made a prison of the world), their caricature of what Humanity should be like in order to be kept in line, taking shape and form in Kindred. Their blood sorcery is almost like a response to the dwindling of magic from the material, a kind of magic that has nothing to do with the Supernal, but instead is of this place.<br /> <br /> But yes, Vampire has a cosmology of its own. Belial is all too real, and a Demon nothing like the rebellious angels of the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T05:00:55-07:00","id":626487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=626125#post626125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there is any specific thing in the books likely to be a player in the Imperial Game, I would say it's that outer darkness. Not any one thing out of it, though perhaps some tales of great things like the Mother of Monsters might reflect encounters with the darkness collectively, conflated into a single being. But there is some darkness eating at the world, and the consequences of its presence are what prevent archmages from expelling its influence.<br /> <br /> You might call that the Curse.<br /> <br /> You might.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if Vampires Sponsor, Crone of her Circle, is personified Darkness. Endless Hunger and Fear. And she <b><i>is</i></b> the Dark Mother of Beasts.<br /> <br /> Both Kindred and Begotten live to sate their Hunger. Both having Maternal figure of Primordial Fear. Both have powers related to Blood of their Kin. Strix could be Heralds of Dark Mother, the Crone itself, in her mad decisions - she IS the Primordial Monsters eating both mortals and her own Children ( of both kinds even ).<br /> <br /> Other solution I have is that Psychomop, Iron Seal of Death, send vampire race on the world to stop natural process of Stygian soul refinement and bound them in vampiric bodies. He made them thirst for blood, so they need to dwindle humanities numbers even more. And as they kill some poor man in violet exsanguination, they left as ghosts - or return as hungry zombie-like vampiric Revenants.<br /> <br /> To be fair, seeing as Dark Mother had many consorts, I would assume they <b>both</b> created first vampires, Mother of Monsters and Psychopomp. And they still look over their Children, in some very wicked way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2015, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T05:04:36-07:00","id":626489,"title":"","content":"Some of Belial's Brood would say it was the Adversary, or the Demiurge. Who could be considered Satan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T02:57:42-07:00","id":627418,"title":"","content":"In my cosmology, there is no united &quot;sponsor&quot; for vampires- instead, there is a loose alliance of many parasitic blood gods who use the strixs as a communication system between themselves and the vampires as some sort of &quot;angels&quot;. Each has its own agenda it wish to advance by using vampires, some a very selfish (like &quot;feed me&quot;) or very world changing (like &quot;creating hell upon earth&quot;). The one to manage that alliance (called &quot;the Coalition of Blood&quot;) is the one to spawn the strixs, so the very ability to participate in the alliance is by acknowledging her (I'm calling her &quot;Lilith&quot; for obvious reasons) and accept her monopoly over the dead. Those who do not obey her, yet dare to play with the undead, are called the &quot;VII Opposition&quot;. The exact list of who belongs to who is kinda blurry, making even high level blood gods fear of betrayal and play political games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T07:38:55-07:00","id":627599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=626446#post626446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever it is, it's content to just let vampires do their thing without interference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which implies it's not the Strix, since they're very much <i>not</i> content to leave Kindred to their own devices. Also, I'd count the Strix as too shallow in their worldview, too low-powered, and too numerous.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd follow the crowd and peg the Crone as the vampires' sponsor (whether or not any particular group of Acolytes is exactly right about what the Crone is). Assuming there is one and it's not just a case of an entire supernatural species having too much inertia to mess with it in any big way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=626487#post626487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Vampires Sponsor, Crone of her Circle, is personified Darkness. Endless Hunger and Fear. And she <b><i>is</i></b> the Dark Mother of Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a triple version of that going. Werewolves descending from a Maiden (who for those who believe this is the Wolf not the Moon), Beasts from a Mother, and vampires from a Crone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T08:56:05-07:00","id":627641,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=627599#post627599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which implies it's not the Strix, since they're very much <i>not</i> content to leave Kindred to their own devices.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Considering their hostility, even if the Strix </span></span></span><i>were </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">splat sponsors, they'd probably be thrilled if an Archmage turned them all to lawnchairs, so odds are it's not them judging by how the Kindred are still around.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=626487#post626487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Other solution I have is that Psychomop, Iron Seal of Death, send vampire race on the world to stop natural process of Stygian soul refinement and bound them in vampiric bodies. He made them thirst for blood, so they need to dwindle humanities numbers even more. And as they kill some poor man in violet exsanguination, they left as ghosts - or return as hungry zombie-like vampiric Revenants.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While totally convincing agenda-wise, I have a gut-level reaction that (judging by the other splat examples) as its own unique Supernal god-thing(s), whatever created vampires would've already existed without the intervention of the Seers. That's a </span></span></span><i>really </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">good conclusion for what the average (Arch)Mage in the street would think, though.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=626487#post626487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Vampires Sponsor, Crone of her Circle, is personified Darkness. Endless Hunger and Fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, while perfectly fitting and appropriate, I have a gut-level feeling that it's not the Crone because the other Covenants are a thing- if vampires have learned anything about the Blood in the last couple thousand years, it's that if you clap your hands hard enough and believe, with enough time and effort and will the Blood will do just about anything short of sit up and beg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T11:08:46-07:00","id":627732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=626475#post626475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given Mage's platonic cosmology, Vampires wouldn't <i>need</i> a sponsor per se. The Supernal is an expanded world of forms, or ideas at their purest, most perfect form. Vampires could be perceived as a corruption of the idea of Humanity. Vampires could be the hubris of the Exarchs' actions (provided they have indeed made a prison of the world), their caricature of what Humanity should be like in order to be kept in line, taking shape and form in Kindred. Their blood sorcery is almost like a response to the dwindling of magic from the material, a kind of magic that has nothing to do with the Supernal, but instead is of this place.<br /> <br /> But yes, Vampire has a cosmology of its own. Belial is all too real, and a Demon nothing like the rebellious angels of the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)The argument falls a little flat when you remember that Archmages can screw around with the Supernal and undo forms and ideas. Archmages could just go in and literally unmake vampirism unless there's someone or something to contest them. Hence, sponsors.<br /> <br /> 2) Eh....It's mixed. This isn't oWoD where each game is a world unto itself. There's nothing that forces you to treat Requiem as though it belongs in the same world as Descent, but the default attitude is that each of the gamelines is an island in the same ocean(Or in the case of Beast, a trade route). So,yes, Vampire has a cosmology of it's own, but it does actually interact with other cosmologies and might have answers in them. Maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T11:23:52-07:00","id":627737,"title":"","content":"Eh, I just go with Caine. Saves time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T12:09:39-07:00","id":627751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=627732#post627732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">each of the gamelines is an island in the same ocean(Or in the case of Beast, a trade route).</div> </div> </div> </div>So in this analogy, would Hunter be pirates?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T12:27:04-07:00","id":627770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=627732#post627732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Eh....It's mixed. This isn't oWoD where each game is a world unto itself. There's nothing that forces you to treat Requiem as though it belongs in the same world as Descent, but the default attitude is that each of the gamelines is an island in the same ocean(Or in the case of Beast, a trade route). So,yes, Vampire has a cosmology of it's own, but it does actually interact with other cosmologies and might have answers in them. Maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except for the Underworld and Hisil. It appears that, because reasons, they exist in the early games but necessarily the latter ones, due to how the game works. I'm completely down with the idea of a the whole &quot;everyone is a separate cosmology,&quot; but we start running into issues of several games trying to claim otherworlds as their domains. Like, Mage claims parts of the Hisil, Underworld, and Astral as theirs, but files the Hedge as crossover material for some reason. Werewolf focuses on the Shadow, doesn't touch the astral, but hints at the Underworld as well.<br /> <br /> Maybe we can say that those games are part of a chain of islands, like Hawaii, while others are more separate? [/random musings]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=627751#post627751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in this analogy, would Hunter be pirates?</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe armies from the mainland? Everyone has mortals as a unified point, so they'd be a mainland. Islands are branches off that mainland. Considering that some hunters are sponsored by the US government and the Church, they might be authorized by the government of the mainland to fight against the islands, which leech off the mainland?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-15-2015, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T12:36:34-07:00","id":627783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1)The argument falls a little flat when you remember that Archmages can screw around with the Supernal and undo forms and ideas. Archmages could just go in and literally unmake vampirism unless there's someone or something to contest them. Hence, sponsors. </div> </div> </div>You didn't really read what they said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Eh....It's mixed. This isn't oWoD where each game is a world unto itself. There's nothing that forces you to treat Requiem as though it belongs in the same world as Descent, but the default attitude is that each of the gamelines is an island in the same ocean(Or in the case of Beast, a trade route). So,yes, Vampire has a cosmology of it's own, but it does actually interact with other cosmologies and might have answers in them. Maybe. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's right at all. It's the reverse in fact. The OWoD games weren't worlds unto themselves, they freely messed with each other and interacted in really important ways.<br /> <br /> The various writers have been pretty blunt that isn't the case in NWoD. The lines make small references to each other here and there, but they generally ignore any broader implications of their cosmologies. Those cosmologies could be made to fit each other, but they aren't written with that in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T12:59:42-07:00","id":627801,"title":"","content":"cWoD was dev as a huge crossover of non-interchangeable parts, at the same time separate and glued. It is a mess, even in the 20ths editions.<br /> <br /> nWoD is a tool box where everything is interchangeable, but at the same time everything is optional. It works.<br /> <br /> I would say the correct answer is that the cosmologies are interchangeable. They don't have to work together, but they can. And that DOES mean that by default they can't directly contradict each other. But they also have to let enough space on canon for you to ignore whatever you want.<br /> <br /> Either way, it is up to the ST and not the goal of the thread. The OP <u>assumes</u> the connection to ask how it could work. Any consideration here only makes sense taking such assumption as true.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it could be manifold.<br /> <br /> First, the Curse itself an be a thing. Whatever created it, the collective curse of the vampires can act as counter-magic. They are just too static, and even more so as a species. Given, that alone wouldn't hold an Archmaster forever, but buy time. Then you could have Methuselahs. I'm up with the idea of powerful enough vampires that could act as splat-sponsors. Even if you don't, powerful Elders would still be resourceful enough to perceive and act against an Archmage focused on destroying the Curse, that's where the time makes difference.<br /> <br /> And you can have a lot of other sponsors out there. Vampirism is a rich source for a lot of Essence, and some pretty awesome spirits can have an invested interest on them. Also other entities interested on the way the vamps do things. None of them would be a sponsor by themselves, but together and with bought time from the very stasis of vampirism, they would accomplish to thwart any attempt to destroy the splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:08:24-07:00","id":627806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=627783#post627783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't really read what they said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no. I actually really did. It just doesn't parse when we're talking about Archamges and the assumptions that come with, namely that both the Fallen and the Supernal worlds are mutable at the influence of other big things. Without something(s) actively fighting for vampires, their position as a natural consequences is something that can be wiped off the slate of eternity.The only other way to read Stylanski's post is to assume the <i>Exarch's are vampire's sponsors</i>, which directly contradicts the idea behind the post, so it's off the table.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think that's right at all. It's the reverse in fact. The OWoD games weren't worlds unto themselves, they freely messed with each other and interacted in really important ways.<br /> <br /> The various writers have been pretty blunt that isn't the case in NWoD. The lines make small references to each other here and there, but they generally ignore any broader implications of their cosmologies. Those cosmologies could be made to fit each other, but they aren't written with that in mind. </div> </div> </div>In the old World, werewolves hated vampires because they were spawn of the Wyrm, and this was canon in Apocalypse, but not in Masquerade. In the new World, werewolves know that vampiresdon't quite fit into their models and have lots of reasons to assume they have something going on in their understanding of themselves, though they occasionally try and figure it out in their paradigm. Likewise, vampires recognize that werewolves are very much their own thing.<br /> <br /> I think you're mistaking &quot;leaving the answers of mysteries to players&quot; as a hard wall between things. That's not the case. Early oWoD was designed with the understanding that you played Masquerade or Oblivion or Apocalypse by themselves, but not together(Ie, you can't play Masquerade,<i>and</i> Oblivion <i>and</i> Apocalypse together at the same time), which is why each gameline could say they had something that appeared in the other and it adhered to the rules of their cosmology. Later oWoD tried to fix that with mixed results. nWoD, by contrast, was written to facilitate crossover from the word go, and resolved clashes of cosmology(such as the way each splat treats the soul) with it's overarching theme of dark mystery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in this analogy, would Hunter be pirates?</div> </div> </div> </div> Maaaaybe? I don't know, islands in a ocean makes sense, but oceanic metaphors aren't really my thing.<br /> <br /> Should have used a desert.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T13:09:41-07:00","id":627808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=627801#post627801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cWoD was dev as a huge crossover of non-interchangeable parts, at the same time separate and glued. It is a mess, even in the 20ths editions.<br /> <br /> nWoD is a tool box where everything is interchangeable, but at the same time everything is optional. It works.<br /> <br /> I would say the correct answer is that the cosmologies are interchangeable. They don't have to work together, but they can. And that DOES mean that by default they can't directly contradict each other. But they also have to let enough space on canon for you to ignore whatever you want.<br /> <br /> Either way, it is up to the ST and not the goal of the thread. The OP <u>assumes</u> the connection to ask how it could work. Any consideration here only makes sense taking such assumption as true.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it could be manifold.<br /> <br /> First, the Curse itself an be a thing. Whatever created it, the collective curse of the vampires can act as counter-magic. They are just too static, and even more so as a species. Given, that alone wouldn't hold an Archmaster forever, but buy time. Then you could have Methuselahs. I'm up with the idea of powerful enough vampires that could act as splat-sponsors. Even if you don't, powerful Elders would still be resourceful enough to perceive and act against an Archmage focused on destroying the Curse, that's where the time makes difference.<br /> <br /> And you can have a lot of other sponsors out there. Vampirism is a rich source for a lot of Essence, and some pretty awesome spirits can have an invested interest on them. Also other entities interested on the way the vamps do things. None of them would be a sponsor by themselves, but together and with bought time from the very stasis of vampirism, they would accomplish to thwart any attempt to destroy the splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T18:03:45-07:00","id":638572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=626487#post626487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other solution I have is that Psychomop, Iron Seal of Death, send vampire race on the world to stop natural process of Stygian soul refinement and bound them in vampiric bodies. He made them thirst for blood, so they need to dwindle humanities numbers even more. And as they kill some poor man in violet exsanguination, they left as ghosts - or return as hungry zombie-like vampiric Revenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't really think the Exarchs exist in any meaningful fashion. Supposedly, in the Atlantis-that-Wasn't, they were Mages who climbed the Celestial Ladder and became Symbols of Tyranny, but who's to say that the Exarchs weren't <i>always</i> such symbols, and the Mages tried to personify them in the original legends so they would have a more concrete opponent than the idealized symbols of tyranny, and that personification took on a life of its own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T08:50:29-07:00","id":639131,"title":"","content":"Hm. Maybe if we asked the question from a different direction it'll shake things up.<br /> <br /> Making an <u>assumption </u>that each big Splat originates or has a sponsor from a different Supernal realm (if for no deeper reason than the dev's seemed to like that kind of symmetry)- for the purposes of <i>this</i> particular hypothetical, what kind of logical or metaphysical or logistical shoehorning would it take for a poster to reasonably justify vampires or their predecessors as being Pandemonic? Is it too convoluted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=638572#post638572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> who's to say that the Exarchs weren't <i>always</i> such symbols, and the Mages tried to personify them in the original legends so they would have a more concrete opponent than the idealized symbols of tyranny, and that personification took on a life of its own?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious- in this case, what would the catalyst be that moved Tyranny to become the dominant Supernal manifestation in the Fallen World, before or after the Abyss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1289,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","user":"Hastur00","date":". 08-25-2015, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T09:26:30-07:00","id":639165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=639131#post639131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making an <u>assumption </u>that each big Splat originates or has a sponsor from a different Supernal realm (if for no deeper reason than the dev's seemed to like that kind of symmetry)- for the purposes of <i>this</i> particular hypothetical, what kind of logical or metaphysical or logistical shoehorning would it take for a poster to reasonably justify vampires or their predecessors as being Pandemonic? Is it too convoluted?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast. The demoniac survival instinct of vampires. Plus so many of the vampire disciplines are based on manipulating the mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T10:10:14-07:00","id":639263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=639165#post639165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Beast. The demoniac survival instinct of vampires. Plus so many of the vampire disciplines are based on manipulating the mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe The Beast is the consort of beast's Dark Mother? It would explained a lot of vampires/beasts parallels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T10:25:34-07:00","id":639274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=639165#post639165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast. The demoniac survival instinct of vampires. Plus so many of the vampire disciplines are based on manipulating the mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just where I was going with it (-D<br /> <br /> But by shoehorning, I meant what could possibly take what should be a chaotically mental and abstract splat and make it so carnal and static and heavily associated with Dea-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=639263#post639263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe The Beast is the consort of beast's Dark Mother? It would explained a lot of vampires/beasts parallels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <i>Now </i>we're cooking with charcoal.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...of course <i>now </i>I'm wondering what an actual Space/Mind splat would be like, because I'm not satisfied by things.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Please disregard that aside.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T11:56:42-07:00","id":639343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=638572#post638572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't really think the Exarchs exist in any meaningful fashion. Supposedly, in the Atlantis-that-Wasn't, they were Mages who climbed the Celestial Ladder and became Symbols of Tyranny, but who's to say that the Exarchs weren't <i>always</i> such symbols, and the Mages tried to personify them in the original legends so they would have a more concrete opponent than the idealized symbols of tyranny, and that personification took on a life of its own?</div> </div> </div> </div> In the Supernal, time is relative, so once you ascend, you exist there for all time. When they went up is meaningless, since you retroactively have existed for all time. By the same token, if the exarchs fall, then its the same as if the symbols never existed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=639131#post639131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Maybe if we asked the question from a different direction it'll shake things up.<br /> <br /> Making an <u>assumption </u>that each big Splat originates or has a sponsor from a different Supernal realm (if for no deeper reason than the dev's seemed to like that kind of symmetry)- for the purposes of <i>this</i> particular hypothetical, what kind of logical or metaphysical or logistical shoehorning would it take for a poster to reasonably justify vampires or their predecessors as being Pandemonic? Is it too convoluted?</div> </div> </div> </div> Who said vampires are associated with Pandemonium? They're more likely associated with the Abyss, considering their ties to the Lower Depths and missing aspects of some Arcana. Primordial has more in common with Pandemonium than Requiem does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm curious- in this case, what would the catalyst be that moved Tyranny to become the dominant Supernal manifestation in the Fallen World, before or after the Abyss? </div> </div> </div> The whole idea of before/after becomes kinda hard to pin down when you're talking about rewriting reality. In either case, the Abyss was formed into the Quintessence/Lie by the Gate, the 11th Exarch, so I'd say &quot;after.&quot; Perhaps, without the Gate, the Abyss would have faded by now, or all we know. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T11:57:28-07:00","id":639345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=639263#post639263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe The Beast is the consort of beast's Dark Mother? It would explained a lot of vampires/beasts parallels.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Dark Mother is the Crone. The God Machine grants Theban;s Miracles. Blessed be, my childe<br /> .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T13:42:22-07:00","id":639418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/626091-are-strix-the-hypothetical-splat-sponsor-from-imperial-mysteries?p=639343#post639343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said vampires are associated with Pandemonium? They're more likely associated with the Abyss, considering their ties to the Lower Depths and missing aspects of some Arcana. </div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no, absolutely*. My headcanon leans toward the Lower Depths-ish in any case. I only chose Pandemonium as a default because of developer symmetry, not metaphysics. It's just that inspecting expected, (or unexpected) symmetries, you can get some really fascinating potential insights, even if you don't discover any kind of &quot;<i>surprise, posters! You were right all along, it IS Pandemonium! Thanks for playing!</i>&quot; near-canon easter egg.<br /> <br /> *especially considering Req.-era Mage saying that the answer for the Arcana of Death's question &quot;is there a soul here&quot; is always &quot;ask again later&quot;. Makes good sense for a creature with an incomplete Death Arcanum to give that question and answer of &quot;undefined&quot;, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T14:57:32-07:00","id":642117,"title":"","content":"But if the strix realm is indeed a lower depth it's pretty clearly one lacking <i>life, </i>not death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T03:41:46-07:00","id":642811,"title":"","content":"As DaveB put it, the things from the lower depths crave and hunger for what they lack. He mentioned Strix lacking and hunger for Vitae (wich is Life).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}